wikipedia_extract: The Japanese destroyer Mikazuki (三日月, ”Crescent Moon”) was one
  of twelve Mutsuki-class destroyers, built for the Imperial Japanese Navy (IJN) during
  the 1920s. At the beginning of the Pacific War, she served in home waters as the
  plane guard for those aircraft carriers that were training or working up. In mid-1942,
  the ship played a minor role in the Battle of Midway and was then assigned to convoy
  escort duties between Formosa and Japan for the next year. Mikazuki was then transferred
  to the Solomon Islands in mid-1943 and was destroyed by American bombers after running
  aground.
